   "source": [
    "## Feature selection\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal is to choose the features the models will use. We compare four methods, because each one has its own point of view:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Correlation** with the price (simple, but only linear).\n",
    "2. **Random Forest importance** (captures non-linear links).\n",
    "3. **Boruta** (keeps a feature only if it does better than random noise).\n",
    "4. **Forward feature selection** (adds features one by one while the score improves).\n",
    "\n",
    "Rules used for all the methods:\n",
    "- The target is `log(price)`, as decided in the cleaning step.\n",
    "- The selection is done on the **train set only**, so the test set stays untouched.\n",
    "- `sqm_price_per_lot` and `sqm_price_per_living` are excluded (they are computed from the price).\n",
    "- `zipcode` is left out of the four methods: it is a category, not a quantity, so a numeric code would mislead them. It is tested separately at the end."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "4ed058e7",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2026-10-08T13:16:33.703502Z",
